Bhola Pulse source packages for Launchpad
=========================================

The signed PPA source builder is intentionally pinned to the immutable
`v0.1.2` release commit:

    009ca2331f2a14159f26a31fe7fa193859676750

Release identity and version-policy metadata live in:

    debian/ppa-release.conf

The upstream archive is created only from that exact release commit and excludes
the top-level `debian/` directory. Debian packaging is then added exclusively
from the clean, committed current `HEAD`. The builder never copies the live
working tree and rejects staged, modified, deleted, or untracked files.

The release builder also refuses when any installed-runtime path differs from
the pinned release snapshot. Pull requests that intentionally change runtime
code continue to use the separate unsigned validation builder:

    bash debian/build-pr-source noble
    bash debian/build-pr-source resolute

Its `~pr1~` source packages exist only to exercise extraction, binary rebuild,
payload inspection, and debhelper-generated systemd lifecycle scripts. They are
never signed or uploaded.

PPA versions for this release are:

    0.1.2-2~ppa1~noble1
    0.1.2-2~ppa1~resolute1

The Debian revision is deliberately `2`: these PPA builds sort newer than the
standalone GitHub package `0.1.2-1`, so an existing installation can move under
APT/PPA management normally. The `~ppa1~...` suffix keeps them older than a
future plain `0.1.2-2` package.

Build unsigned source uploads from the repository root:

    bash debian/build-ppa-source noble
    bash debian/build-ppa-source resolute

The Noble upload includes `bhola-pulse_0.1.2.orig.tar.xz`. The Resolute upload
is built with `-sd` and reuses the identical upstream archive after Noble has
been accepted by Launchpad.

Before upload:

1. inspect the generated `.dsc`, `_source.changes`, and `_source.buildinfo`;
2. verify all checksums and the Distribution/Version fields;
3. sign each `_source.changes` file with the OpenPGP key associated with the
   Launchpad account;
4. upload only the signed source package to:

       ppa:lbudzynowski/apps

Launchpad builds the binary packages. Do not upload a locally built `.deb` as a
PPA source upload. No signing key, passphrase, token, private path, or generated
source artifact belongs in the repository or CI logs.
